WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
A homeowner spots a leak.

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.740
They send an inquiry to three roofing
companies.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.960
The first one to respond has the best
chance of winning the job.

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.220
Will it be yours?

5
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.660
When your team is on a roof, inquiries can
sit in an inbox.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.920
By the time someone reads them, the
customer may have moved on.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.980
Roofline keeps the conversation moving.

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.380
The customer fills in a simple form and
roofline checks where they are, what

9
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.660
work they need, and how urgent it is.

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.960
It saves the details and alerts your team
so they know who to contact and why.

11
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.940
The customer receives an immediate
acknowledgement.

12
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.720
If they've asked for a text, roofline
follows up by SMS and records what

13
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.440
happened without sending the same message
twice.

14
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.660
Less time sorting inquiries,

15
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.700
fewer missed opportunities,

16
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.960
and a customer who knows you've heard
them.

17
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.120
Roofline.

18
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.020
A faster response when it matters most.

19
00:00:59.060 --> 00:00:59.360
Roofline.

20
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.260
Built by Mark Automates.

21
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:02.980
A little less admin.

22
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.040
A lot more time to do the work that
matters.
